# Discuit (bees — podman quadlet; see hosts/bees/discuit.nix).
# XFF is PINNED to ::1, deliberately: Discuit stores client IPs in
# MariaDB INET6 columns, and debian MariaDB 10.11 rejects plain-IPv4
# strings from the app's prepared statements (Error 1292, signup-
# breaking — sql_mode relaxation does not help the binary protocol).
# A valid IPv6 literal keeps every IP-writing path happy; real client
# IPs are lost, which is fine on an overlay-private instance where
# every client is caddy-on-loopback anyway.
@discuit host discuit.internal.crussell.io
handle @discuit {
    reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8100 {
        header_up X-Forwarded-For "::1"
    }
}
